course: dictionary
lesson: 7327
title: The word planet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A planet is a very large round object in space that moves around a star. Our Earth is a planet, and it moves around the Sun. Read the words around planet to check its meaning: «The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer its year» tells you a planet travels around the Sun.
explain: Planet can also mean our Earth, as in «Look after the planet». Which meaning fits? When people talk about saving it, they mean the Earth. When they talk about years, orbits or the Sun, they mean a round object in space.
explain: Careful: «A planetary nebula has nothing to do with planets». The word planetary here is a cloud of gas, named because it looked like a round planet through old telescopes. The clue is in the words «has nothing to do with».
fact: A planet is a very large round object in space that moves around a star.
fact: Our Solar System has eight planets in order from the Sun: Mercury, Venus, Earth, Mars, Jupiter, Saturn, Uranus and Neptune.
fact: Jupiter is the biggest planet in our Solar System.
fact: Planets do not make their own light; they reflect the light of the Sun.
fact: «Save the planet» means look after the Earth, for example by recycling and saving energy.
exercise: «The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer its year.» In this sentence, what is a planet? | A kind of telescope | A cloud of gas in space | A type of spotlight | *A very large round object that moves around the Sun
exercise: «Look after the planet» means what? | *Look after the Earth, our home | Look after the Sun | Look after a telescope | Look at the stars at night
exercise: Which planet is the biggest in our Solar System? | *Jupiter | Mars | Neptune | Mercury
test: Which of these is a planet in our Solar System? | Moon | Sun | *Saturn | Star
test: Why can we see planets shining in the night sky? | They are powered by a star's fire | They are lit by the Moon | *They reflect the light of the Sun | They make their own bright light
exam: Which phrase uses planet to mean our Earth? | Mars is the Red Planet | Pluto is now a dwarf planet | A planetary nebula is a cloud of gas | *Look after the planet, and recycle
